    @@ README.md: sources: []
      
      Moving a repository or changing its worktree root requires reconciling existing worktree paths and Git metadata. A configuration edit does not move them.
      
    --Every `akrogon next` pass reconciles worktrees, scratch and run roots against leaf state: clean, reachable, unused leftovers are removed. Everything it keeps shows under each repo in plain `akrogon status` as `Kept by last cleanup:` lines for paths that still exist, and `akrogon status <slug>` prints the whole kept report as `Kept:` lines with path and reason.
    -+Every `akrogon next` pass reconciles worktrees, scratch and run roots against leaf state: clean, reachable, unused leftovers are removed. `verify-*`, `batch-*` and `<slug>-u<N>` copies in the worktree store are scratch, removed with `git worktree remove --force` once the owner is gone (an ended or dead verify run, an absent or dead `batch-<id>.owner` build record, a merged owner leaf) and kept while the owner lives, while a live pane or a surviving process sits inside, or while the pane list is unavailable. Everything it keeps shows under each repo in plain `akrogon status` as `Kept by last cleanup:` lines for paths that still exist, and `akrogon status <slug>` prints the whole kept report as `Kept:` lines with path and reason.
    +-Every `akrogon next` pass reconciles worktrees, scratch and run roots against leaf state: clean, reachable, unused leftovers are removed. The same pass stops the systemd slice of a merged or failed leaf once its tab is gone — ending processes it left running — unless a live run record names the slice or the pass itself runs inside it; a loaded `akrogon-l*` slice matching no leaf record is stopped only when it holds no process, and failed `akrogon-run-*` units are cleared. Everything it keeps shows under each repo in plain `akrogon status` as `Kept by last cleanup:` lines for paths that still exist, and `akrogon status <slug>` prints the whole kept report as `Kept:` lines with path and reason.
    ++Every `akrogon next` pass reconciles worktrees, scratch and run roots against leaf state: clean, reachable, unused leftovers are removed. The same pass stops the systemd slice of a merged or failed leaf once its tab is gone — ending processes it left running — unless a live run record names the slice or the pass itself runs inside it; a loaded `akrogon-l*` slice matching no leaf record is stopped only when it holds no process, and failed `akrogon-run-*` units are cleared. `verify-*`, `batch-*` and `<slug>-u<N>` copies in the worktree store are scratch, removed with `git worktree remove --force` once the owner is gone (an ended or dead verify run, an absent or dead `batch-<id>.owner` build record, a merged owner leaf) and kept while the owner lives, while a live pane or a surviving process sits inside, or while the pane list is unavailable. Everything it keeps shows under each repo in plain `akrogon status` as `Kept by last cleanup:` lines for paths that still exist, and `akrogon status <slug>` prints the whole kept report as `Kept:` lines with path and reason.
      
      This repository's [reference index](docs/reference-index.md) links its code areas.
      
     
      ## src/AREA.md ##
     @@
    - - `src/verify.ts` checks a commit out detached, runs every command for the caller's scope, logs each into the leaf or holder and records one receipt in `issues/verify-runs.jsonl`; `requireGreenReceipt` is the one gate the `check.review` move, the `check.repair` move into `merge`, `merged --check` stamping and direct-guards call.
      - `src/admission.ts` registers each run's record under `<globalHome>/runs/`, sweeps stale records and their run units, and admits at once — a matching `AKROGON_RUN` token of a live run is the nested case that creates nothing; the memory reading and spacing were dropped 2026-10-14.
    - - `src/scope.ts` names the per-leaf slice (`leafSlice`, used by `src/stop.ts`), pane scopes and `akrogon-run-<id>` run units, moves a pane shell into its scope with busctl `StartTransientUnit`, and checks it read-only through `AKROGON_PROC_ROOT` (default `/proc`); `allocate` in `src/next.ts` closes a recorded pane outside its scope and boxes every pane before the seat starts. `src/stop-run.ts` stops the run units live records tie to the caller's scope. `src/stop.ts` keeps the host-local `stopped.yaml` record and runs `stop`/`start`; dispatch, the merge queue and status read it.
    --- `src/reconcile.ts` removes dead worktrees, scratch and run roots each pass and writes the kept report `status` prints under the ignored `reconcile/` state dir.
    -+- `src/reconcile.ts` removes dead worktrees, scratch and run roots each pass — `verify-*`, `batch-*` and `<slug>-u<N>` store copies go by owner state (`batch-<id>.owner` record for batch copies) behind live-pane and surviving-process vetoes — and writes the kept report `status` prints under the ignored `reconcile/` state dir.
    + - `src/scope.ts` names the per-leaf slice (`leafSlice`, used by `src/stop.ts`), pane scopes and `akrogon-run-<id>` run units, moves a pane shell into its scope with busctl `StartTransientUnit`, and checks it read-only through `AKROGON_PROC_ROOT` (default `/proc`) and `AKROGON_CGROUP_ROOT` (default `/sys/fs/cgroup`); `allocate` in `src/next.ts` closes a recorded pane outside its scope and boxes every pane before the seat starts. `src/stop-run.ts` stops the run units live records tie to the caller's scope. `src/stop.ts` keeps the host-local `stopped.yaml` record and runs `stop`/`start`; dispatch, the merge queue and status read it.
    + - `src/evidence.ts` maps a recorded log path to its bytes (`locate`, `readMember`, `readLog`, `readLogAcross`): plain file first, then the owner's `evidence.tar.zst`; `akrogon log` and `src/flaky.ts` read through it.
    +-- `src/reconcile.ts` removes dead worktrees, scratch and run roots each pass, stops finished-leaf slices and unmatched empty `akrogon-l*` slices, clears failed `akrogon-run-*` units in the host step, and writes the kept reports `status` prints under the ignored `reconcile/` state dir and `reconcile-host.json`.
    ++- `src/reconcile.ts` removes dead worktrees, scratch and run roots each pass — `verify-*`, `batch-*` and `<slug>-u<N>` store copies go by owner state (`batch-<id>.owner` record for batch copies) behind live-pane and surviving-process vetoes — stops finished-leaf slices and unmatched empty `akrogon-l*` slices, clears failed `akrogon-run-*` units in the host step, and writes the kept reports `status` prints under the ignored `reconcile/` state dir and `reconcile-host.json`.
      
